  "query_preview": "..\n\nAfternoon cumulus is mixed with a mid level cloud component tied to \nmoisture transport aloft while surface high pressure is otherwise \nthe primary weather influence across Lower Mi today. The high \npressure air mass combined with the mix of clouds and sun are \nproducing pleasant conditions across the region that continue \ntonight. Cloud production will be variable as mid level flow remains \nweak and theta-e disorganized, however periods of clear sky have \nadequate duration for enough cooling to reach low temperatures in \nthe mid to upper 50s outside of metro Detroit. Beside the clouds, an \nuptick in south wind occurs before sunrise which is just enough to \nkeep readings a few degrees warmer than this morning, which even saw \nsome 40s in the typically cooler locations around the region. \n\nHigh pressure departs to the Atlantic coast while the next low \npressure system organizes across the high Plains during Saturday. \nThese are the primary surface weather elements connected by the \nupper jet spanning the Canadian border from Montana to the northern \nGreat Lakes. It's the upper jet that boosts moisture transport with \nmuch farther eastward reach into Lower Mi compared to the warm front \nfrom late Saturday through Saturday night. This results in a renewed \ncloud increase during the afternoon and an increasing chance of \nshowers and thunderstorms Saturday night into Sunday morning. \nConvective potential ramps up considerably on low level jet strength \nin the northern Plains and upper Midwest tonight and again Saturday \nnight as the 850-700 mb theta-e ridge builds west to east into Lower \nMi. The inbound moisture axis helps improve prospects that \nconvective remnants survive into SE Mi by Sunday morning. Clouds and \nshowers then linger during the day as the warm front moves in ahead \nof the Plains to Midwest low pressure system. The preferred forecast \nleans toward higher POPs and lower temperatures compared to NBM to \nfinish the weekend. \n\nToday's 12Z deterministic/AI/ensemble means show the northward \nprogress of the surface warm front is still a forecast focus for \nMonday. Consensus slightly favors the front moving into the northern \nGreat Lakes followed by a new round of heat and humidity that builds \ninto at least the southern part of Lower Mi for the early week \nperiod.",
